# The cleaned trip table is large and exactly reproducible by re-running
# `EDA/01_data_cleaning.py`, so no policy variant is tracked.  The glob covers
# the tagged wider-policy outputs (trips_clean_keepzerodur_keepanomday...).
# The small siblings (cell_summary*, cleaning_report*, cleaning_summary*) still
# follow the rest of out/ and stay trackable.
EDA/out/trips_clean*.csv.gz

# External reference dataset used to verify the cleaning fix (XGBoost README §0);
# large and not needed to run anything.
/trips_clean_keepzerodur_keepanomday.csv.gz

# --- Large, regenerable artefacts -------------------------------------------
# These rules exist because of size, not because the files are useless: each is
# either a redundant copy of a tracked input or something a tracked script
# rebuilds, so a clone can reproduce it — but carrying it made `git pull` slow
# for everyone on the repository.
#
# The 34 MB vendor export.  Same 667,821 trips as xgb_bikeflow's cleaned,
# tracked extract; one test compares the two and skips when this file is
# absent.  See xgb_bikeflow/README.md "Where the data comes from".
xgb_bikeflow/data/dataset_train_20260921_lsz.csv.gz

# A whole-repository archive; /Dataset is the raw input directory (also above).
EDA.zip

